==========================================
CLOUD/DEVOPS DAY 04 NOTES — Lambda Functions
Date: 26-11-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- Lambda runs code without me managing a server - but a server still exists, AWS just hides it
- Code must be zipped before upload; --handler tells Lambda which file.function to call first
- event = the input data passed to the function (from --payload here, or a trigger on real AWS)
- A Lambda function needs an IAM role (reused Day 03's Day03LambdaExecutionRole) to actually run
- invoke can be tested repeatedly with different payloads without redeploying anything
- Log groups are created automatically per function for debugging

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] zip function.zip handler.py
[ ] awslocal lambda create-function --role arn:...Day03LambdaExecutionRole
[ ] awslocal lambda invoke --payload '{"name": "..."}' response.json
[ ] awslocal logs describe-log-groups
[ ] awslocal lambda delete-function

paste your real output here :
$ awslocal lambda invoke --function-name Day04HelloFunction --payload '{"name": "Cloud Day 4"}' --cli-binary-format raw-in-base64-out response.json
$ cat response.json
